<% content_for :title, "Pixel Privacy · Lilly Bit Games" %>
<article class="policy-page">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p>Pixel is a drawing guessing game operated by LILLY BIT LLC, doing business as Lilly Bit Games. Updated October 15, 2026.</p>
  <h2>Playing Pixel</h2>
  <p>The mobile apps use an anonymous player profile. You can choose a nickname; no email address or password is required. We store your player identifier, nickname, rooms, game settings, scores, and timestamps to run games and let you return to a room. Guesses are sent to our server to check answers. They may appear in service logs.</p>
  <p>Players in a shared room can see each other's nicknames and scores. Anyone you share an invite with can join the room while it is available. Do not use private information as a nickname or guess.</p>
  <h2>Devices and service providers</h2>
  <p>Our server receives IP addresses, browser or app information, and request logs for security and service operation. The app saves your nickname, game choices, and last room on your device. Your player credential is stored using iOS Keychain or encrypted Android storage. Data is sent over HTTPS.</p>
  <p>Our hosting and infrastructure providers process data to operate Pixel. OpenAI generates drawings from our curated game prompts; we do not send your nickname, player credential, or guesses to OpenAI to generate drawings. The mobile apps include no advertising or analytics SDK, do not track you across other apps, and do not sell your personal data.</p>
  <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
  <p>Game and player records are retained until removed; they do not currently expire automatically. Security logs and backups may be retained by our infrastructure providers. Uninstalling the app does not delete server records.</p>
  <p id="delete-data">To request access to or deletion of your Pixel data, email <a href="mailto:hello@lillybitgames.com?subject=Pixel%20data%20request">hello@lillybitgames.com</a> with your nickname and a room invite link, if available. Do not send a password or player credential. We may ask for information to verify which records are yours. We will remove or anonymize identifiable records after verification, subject to necessary security and legal retention. A request may affect your ability to return to old rooms.</p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>If you contact support, we receive your email address and the information you choose to provide and use it to respond. Pixel is intended for a general audience, not directed at children under 13. Contact us if you believe a child has provided personal information.</p>
  <p><a href="mailto:hello@lillybitgames.com">hello@lillybitgames.com</a> · <%= link_to "Support", support_path %></p>
</article>
